<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Saloum</h1><p class="st-meta">1494 CE – 1891 CE (approx.) · capital Kahone</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Serer and Wolof kingdom of the Saloum delta in Senegal, rich from salt and trade, ruled by the Guelowar dynasty from Kahone.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Saloum was founded around 1494 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbegan-ndour">Mbegan Ndour</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serer">Serer</a> warrior linked through his mother to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guelowar">Guelowar</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-sine">Kingdom of Sine</a>, who according to tradition killed Eli <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banabhatta">Bana</a>, the Muslim cleric then ruling the region. The capital was set at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kahone">Kahone</a>, near present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaolack">Kaolack</a>, and the kingdom broke free of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a> in the following decades.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Buur Saloum ruled with a council of great titled chiefs and the Lingeer, a royal woman of high rank. Saloum controlled salt pans in the delta and trade routes to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-gambia">Gambia</a> river, and became the most extensive Serer-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> state. In the 1860s the jihadist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maba-diakhou-ba">Maba Diakhou Ba</a> conquered much of it, spreading <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> made Saloum a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> and absorbed it into the colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-senegal">French Senegal</a> in 1891. Its kings served as colonial chiefs until the monarchy lapsed in the 20th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaolack">Kaolack</a> became a centre of the groundnut trade.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-saloum.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Saloum" width="320" height="224"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kingdom_of_Saloum_Map.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1494 CE – 1891 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kahone</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mbegan Ndour</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Serer religion and Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serer and Wolof</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/senegal">Senegal</a>, <a href="/countries/gambia">Gambia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Saloum, Saluum</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1692&amp;focus=kingdom-of-saloum" aria-label="Kingdom of Saloum on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4241 1650 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Saloum lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4561 1906L4587 1861M4561 1906L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4587 1861h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4561 1906h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4561 1906h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kahone. <a href="/atlas?year=1692&amp;focus=kingdom-of-saloum">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

